{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1957 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "230b493e9300a7917fcc15c29c2fba402fa8d649fb7bbe9844b789abcb30ad5c" :edb/db-before-t 1956 :edb/db-after-t 1957 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535269 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:56:36.747Z" 13194139535269 true] [17592186192299 1100 "Compute $P\\left( 1 \\lt   X \\lt 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/assets/394c60a510e39043cda5072c0b57a663b200275035d72c15f20c5a257e6c4fc0.png)" 13194139535269 true] [17592186192299 1100 "Compute $P\\left(1 \\lt X \\lt 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n${\\frac{1}{18}(x^{2} - 1),\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$." 13194139535269 false] [17592186192299 1145 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$, then\n\n$$\nP(a \\lt X \\lt b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1 < X < 3) &= ∫_{1}^{3}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{18}(x^{2} - 1)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}∫_{1}^{3}(x^{2} - 1)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}[\\frac{1}{3}x^{3} - x]_{1}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}([\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3} - (3)] - [\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3} - (1)]) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}([9 - 3] - [\\frac{1}{3} - 1]) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}(6 + \\frac{2}{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18} \\cdot \\frac{20}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{10}{27}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535269 false] [17592186192299 1145 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\lt   X \\lt      b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{18}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{\\int }_{1}^{3}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-x]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}([\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3}-(3)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}-(1)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}([9-3]-[\\frac{1}{3}-1]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}(6+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}\\cdot \\frac{20}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535269 true] [17592186192339 1100 "Compute $P\\left(  X \\leq 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/assets/1cd6271fdb46d54db66d2b4f5acd10146f42a0dd64a3326ea7e53e07d4915633.png)" 13194139535269 true] [17592186192339 1100 "Compute $P\\left(X \\leq 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n${\\frac{2x}{45},\\begin{vmatrix}2 \\le x \\le 7, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$." 13194139535269 false] [17592186192339 1145 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$, then\n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x \\lt 2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X \\le 3) &= ∫_{2}^{3}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x}{45}dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{45}x^{2}]_{2}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{45}(3^{2} - 2^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{45} \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535269 false] [17592186192339 1145 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq  b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x \\lt  2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x}{45}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{45}\\,{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}({3}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535269 true] [17592186192340 1100 "Compute $P\\left( 2 \\leq          X \\leq          4 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040290/assets/e01b36a6a2b00b47ce36b59d5b3e1a4fea4cbc26b0b7d46d60e40638161982d8.png)" 13194139535269 true] [17592186192340 1100 "Compute $P\\left(2 \\leq X \\leq 4 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n${\\frac{1}{9}x,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x < 3, \\\\ x - 3,\\end{vmatrix}3 \\le x \\le 4,; 0, \\mid otherwise$." 13194139535269 false] [17592186192340 1145 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$, then\n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(2 \\le X \\le 4) &= ∫_{2}^{4}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{9}xdx + ∫_{3}^{4}(x - 3)dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{18}x^{2}]_{2}^{3} + [\\frac{1}{2}x^{2} - 3x]_{3}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}[3^{2} - 2^{2}] + ([\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2} - 3(4)] - [\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2} - 3(3)]) \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{18} - 4 + \\frac{9}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{14}{18} \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535269 false] [17592186192340 1145 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\leq        X \\leq        b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 4) & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{9}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}(x-3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{18}{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{3}+{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-3x]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}[{3}^{2}-{2}^{2}]+([\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2}-3(4)]-[\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2}-3(3)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{18}-4+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535269 true] [17592186192578 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340903 13194139535269 true] [17592186192578 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340917 13194139535269 